Input: {"question": "378th refers to which type of unit?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 0, "end": 92, "text": "378th Fighter Squadron The 378th Fighter Squadron is an active United States Air Force unit."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 93, "end": 189, "text": "It is assigned to the 495th Fighter Group, Ninth Air Force, stationed at Truax Field, Wisconsin."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 190, "end": 231, "text": "It was last activated on 8 November 2015."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 232, "end": 352, "text": "Established on 1 March 1943 at Westover Field, Massachusetts as the 362d Fighter Group, equipped with P-47 Thunderbolts."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 353, "end": 450, "text": "Deployed to the European Theater of Operations (ETO), and assigned to Ninth Air Force in England."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 451, "end": 495, "text": "Engaged in combat operations until May 1945."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d00", "start": 496, "end": 622, "text": "Reassigned back to the United States in August–September 1945, and assigned to First Air Force at Seymour Johnson Field, North"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d01", "start": 0, "end": 106, "text": "378th Troop Carrier Squadron The 378th Troop Carrier Squadron is an inactive United States Air Force unit."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d01", "start": 107, "end": 159, "text": "It was last assigned to the 60th Troop Carrier Wing."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d01", "start": 160, "end": 238, "text": "It was inactivated at Dreux-Louvilliers Air Base, France on 25 September 1958."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d01", "start": 239, "end": 343, "text": "Established as a B-25 Mitchell medium bombardment squadron in early 1942; trained under Third Air Force."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d01", "start": 344, "end": 621, "text": "Assigned to Columbia Army Air Base, South Carolina as first an Operational Training Unit (OTU) for newly formed squadrons, then in 1943 becoming a Replacement Training Unit (RTU) for pilots and aircrew on the B-25 prior to the personnel being assigned overseas to combat units."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d02", "start": 0, "end": 99, "text": "unit, it was equipped with Douglas O-46 and North American O-47 single-engine observation aircraft."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d02", "start": 100, "end": 185, "text": "The group conducted its operations along the southeastern coast of the United States."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d02", "start": 186, "end": 262, "text": "Only the 523d Squadron was located with the group's headquarters at Langley."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d02", "start": 263, "end": 412, "text": "The 520th Squadron operated from Jacksonville Municipal Airport, Florida, while the 521st was stationed at Charleston Army Air Field, South Carolina."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d02", "start": 413, "end": 609, "text": "In late November, Army Air Forces Antisubmarine Command began a series of organizational actions to more nearly align it with United States Navy headquarters engaged in the antisubmarine campaign."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d02", "start": 610, "end": 683, "text": "On 20 November, the 522d Bombardment Squadron at Lantana Airport, Florida"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d03", "start": 0, "end": 392, "text": "as the 378th Bombardment Group ( Medium ) on 13 October 1942 Activated on 18 December 1942 Inactivated on 14 December 1942 [ 27 ] Redesignated 378th Air Expeditionary Group and converted to provisional status on 24 October 2005 [ 1 ] Activated on 2 August 2019 [ 9 ] Redesignated 378th Air Expeditionary Wing on 14 November 2019 [ 1 ] It operates out of Prince Sultan Airbase , Saudi Arabia ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d03", "start": 393, "end": 519, "text": "[ 28 ] Assignments [ edit ] Army Air Forces Antisubmarine Command , 13 October — 14 December 1942 [ 5 ] Air Combat Command , 2"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d04", "start": 0, "end": 94, "text": "378th Bombardment Group | Military Wiki | Fandom Start a Wiki Sign In Do n't have an account ?"}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d04", "start": 95, "end": 510, "text": "Register Sign In Military Wiki Explore Main Page Discuss All Pages Community Interactive Maps Popular pages Most visited articles Military ranks of the Philippines List of currently active United States military land vehicles Project maintenance Double redirects Broken redirects Wanted categories Wanted pages Wanted templates Uncategorized Categories Short pages Unused categories Sign In Do n't have an account ?"}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d04", "start": 511, "end": 657, "text": "Register Sign In Explore Fan Central Current Skip to content Military 353,117 pages Explore Main Page Discuss All Pages Community Interactive Maps"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0436-691ecb22e4be:d05", "start": 0, "end": 102, "text": "DVIDS - 378th Air Expeditionary Wing Maintenance window scheduled to begin at February 14th 2200 est ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, 